Anisakys — Alembic Migrations
==============================

Alembic is the ONLY place where the database schema is defined. The
application never creates or alters tables at runtime: on startup it checks
that the database is at the latest revision and refuses to start otherwise
(src/database/schema.py: ensure_schema_is_current).

Apply all pending migrations:
    alembic upgrade head

Print the SQL instead of running it (for review by a DBA):
    alembic upgrade head --sql

Rollback one migration:
    alembic downgrade -1

Show current revision / history:
    alembic current
    alembic history

Create a new migration (hand-written SQL, there are no ORM models):
    alembic revision -m "describe the change"
Revision ids are short sequential strings ("001", "002", "003", ...): set
`revision` and `down_revision` accordingly and use IF NOT EXISTS / guarded
DO blocks so the migration is idempotent.

Database URL resolution (see alembic/env.py): DATABASE_URL environment
variable, else DATABASE_URL in the env file named by ANISAKYS_ENV_FILE, else
.env.test under pytest, else .env.
